# Figures

Data figures are generated from scripts; diagrams are declarative JSON
exported by trazo. Both are referenced from the manuscript.

```bash
scripts/trazo build --prepare=inputs        # figures/scripts -> figures/output/
scripts/trazo diagram export --all          # figures/diagrams/*.json -> figures/external/
scripts/trazo diagram check --all --exports # lint; fail if an export is missing or stale
```

The diagram editor is part of the live preview, at `/diagrams`: run
`scripts/trazo preview serve` after the build above.

| Output | Source | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
{% if example %}| `figures/output/png/fig1_trend.png` | `figures/scripts/fig1_trend.py` | Example data figure |
| `figures/external/fig2_workflow.png` | `figures/diagrams/fig2_workflow.json` | Example diagram |
{% else %}| `figures/output/png/fig1_name.png` | `figures/scripts/fig1_name.py` | Replace with each figure |
{% endif %}
- `figures/style/tokens.json`: colours, fonts, text styles and strokes
  used by diagrams (and available to figure scripts).
- `figures/fonts/`: fonts embedded in diagram exports (SIL OFL).

Do not edit files in `figures/output/` or `figures/external/` by hand.
Update the script or the diagram JSON and regenerate.
